# Tech Stack

This is a Nuxt 4 project built with TypeScript. That means auto imports are available for everything that would be manually imported in a regular Vue project.

NuxtUI v4 is used for the UI. Global customizations are preferred over local prop overrides, unless the use case is unique to the instance. Global modifications are done in `@/app/config/nuxt-ui/`. Work with NuxtUI is facilitated by the usage of the official NuxtUI MCP, so make sure to use it in prompts as much as possible.

Image optimization is made possible with Nuxt Image.

Icons used throughout the project either come from the Lucide icon set, or custom icons stored in `@/app/assets/icons`. These are imported using iconsMap from `@/app/utils/iconsMap`.

VueUse is used for various utility functions.

ESLint and Prettier are used for linting and formatting. There's also the `.editorconfig` file for less common file types.

The back-end is constructed using Nuxt Nitro and the code resides in `@/server`.
